  "path": "full",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "g_n(t) \\;=\\; \\frac{t^n - n\\,t + (n-1)}{(t-1)^2}.",
    "plain": "The parent fixes the *sharp left endpoint* `a_n^*` of the region where the strict Bernoulli inequality holds for odd exponents. This leaf asks two concrete things: (1) show that on `(-∞, -1)` the relevant polynomial factor has exactly one root, so `a_n^*` is well defined as that unique root; and (2) prove the sharp asymptotic that this endpoint sits just below `-2`, approaching `-2` at rate `Θ(1/n)` as the odd exponent grows.",
